The `abletonosc/` and `pythonosc/` directories are unmodified upstream code.
`__init__.py` and `manager.py` are also unmodified upstream code, vendored
alongside `abletonosc/` because `__init__.py` does `from .manager import
Manager`; without `manager.py` the Remote Script cannot construct its
Manager instance inside Live. (The brief's copy list omitted `manager.py`;
this is the one deviation from it, made because Tasks 2 and later require a
working Remote Script, not just an importable `abletonosc.handler` module.)

The upstream `client/` directory (a standalone CLI/test client) is not
vendored: nothing in `abletonosc/`, `manager.py`, or `__init__.py` imports
it, so it is not needed for the Remote Script to run inside Live.

Our additions live in `copilot/`. Do not edit vendored files in place; add a
handler in `copilot/` and register it from `__init__.py` instead.
